{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["ותכס — her head." "בצעיף — for this is not the way of widows." "ותתעלף — she covered her face so that Yehudah would not recognize her." "בפתח עינים — at the gate of a crossroads where everyone passes through and is visible to the eyes by way of there, and the one who explains עינים as a city is mistaken. For it is written before us היא בעינים, and if there were a city there, it should have said בעינים with a hatef bet — a shva, for we do not find that one says בית אל ביריחו בירושלים with a qamatz."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {3 "The comment on vocalization is terse: Rashbam argues that if עינים were a place name, the bet-prefix would take shva (hatef), as seen in בית אל, ביריחו, בירושלים, rather than qamatz. The final parenthetical בקמץ appears to gloss that these examples all lack qamatz under the bet; the text may be slightly compressed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:38.674754003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}